++On i915 GPUs, overall render and shared video utilization are also available through PMU engine-busy counters, including on GPUs whose fdinfo does not expose engine times.
++
++Intel requires CAP_PERFMON or CAP_SYS_ADMIN capabilities to access the total memory usage, an accurate GPU frequency, and PMU utilization counters.
++After installing NVTOP as root (for example, at `/usr/local/bin/nvtop`), you can grant the necessary permission to that exact file with `sudo setcap cap_perfmon=ep /usr/local/bin/nvtop`.
